 # kvasok-site
 
-One-page website of Kvások & syn, a fictional family bakery (claude-crews example). Express + TypeScript, server-rendered HTML, no database yet.
+One-page website of Kvások & syn, a fictional family bakery (claude-crews example). Express + TypeScript, server-rendered HTML, no database (orders live in a JSON file). Visitors can contact the shop and order bread and cakes for pickup, paid at pickup.
 
 ## Commands
 
 - `npm test`: vitest + supertest (`test/`)
 - `npm run typecheck`: `tsc --noEmit`
 - `npm run dev`: dev server on :3000 (stop it when done)
+- `npm start`: same server with `NODE_ENV=production` (Express only; `index.ts` still uses `ConsoleMailer`)
+- Env: `PORT` (3000), `ORDERS_FILE` (`data/orders.json`, `data/` is gitignored), `SHOP_EMAIL`
 
 ## Map
 
-- `src/app.ts`: routes (`GET /`, `POST /contact`); `createApp({ mailer })` so tests inject a fake mailer
+- `src/app.ts`: routes `GET /` (also `?order=ID` confirmation), `POST /contact`, `POST /order`; `createApp({ mailer, orders, now })` so tests inject a fake mailer, store and clock
 - `src/render.ts`: the page as a template string; always pass user input through `escapeHtml`
-- `src/menu.ts`: products and prices in cents; `src/hours.ts`: opening hours and time zone
+- `src/menu.ts`: products and prices in cents; `src/hours.ts`: opening hours, `CLOSED_DATES` (holidays), time zone
+- `src/slots.ts`: slot generation, cut-off, business-rule constants
+- `src/orders.ts`: `Order`, `OrderStore`, `InMemoryOrderStore`, `FileOrderStore`, pricing, shop/customer mail builders
 - `src/i18n.ts` + `src/locales/{sk,en}.json`: every visible string exists in both locales
 - `src/mailer.ts`: `Mailer` interface; `ConsoleMailer` in development
 
 ## Rules
 
 - Validate every form with zod; on error re-render the page with status 400 and the escaped values.
-- Times are local to `Europe/Bratislava`.
-- Prices are integers in cents.
+- Times are local to `Europe/Bratislava`. Slot ids are local wall time `"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM"`. `localNow` in `slots.ts` is the only time zone conversion; never use `Date#getDay`/`getHours` or add 86400000 (use `addDays`).
+- Prices are integers in cents and come from `MENU` on the server only, never from the form.
+- Business rules are constants in `slots.ts`: 8 orders per 30-minute slot, 14-day horizon, cut-off at min(14:00, closing time) on the last open day before the pickup day, cakes need 2 days' notice and max 3, max 20 per item, max 3 open future orders per email.
+- `OrderStore` methods stay synchronous, and `reserve()` must check and insert atomically.
+- Express 4 does not catch async rejections: async handlers wrap everything in try/catch and call `next(err)`.
+- Both forms have a honeypot field; the order form also has a resubmission token (same token and same content is not a new order).
+- `data/orders.json` is read at startup only. Hand-edit it (e.g. set `"status": "cancelled"` to free a slot) only while the server is stopped, or the next order overwrites it.
+- `FileOrderStore` is single-process only.
